-- title:
--   Gauss prime strictly inside a supersingular chart-algebra point
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q$ and $\ell$ with $q\ge 5$, $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\neq q$, and a natural number $M'\neq 0$ divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((T))$ (`LaurentSeries L`) which, by `hK`, is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((T))$ generated by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the rational function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and subgroup $H=\,$[`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/(q\ell))^\times$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain, henselian local with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an algebra structure over which it is a fraction-ring presentation of $L$, and let $K$ carry a compatible $A$-algebra structure (scalar tower $A\to L\to K$). Assume $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and that $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`). Let $j\in K$ be an element whose Laurent series is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (`hj`), with $j\neq 0$ as a `Fact`. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the $A$-subalgebra `chartAlg A ↥K {j}` of $K$ attached to the one-element set $\{j\}$, and `jChartFin` for $j$ viewed in $C$.
--
--   Let $y\subseteq C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ (with decidable equality) and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   Next come the data on the two-chart integral model $X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout scheme glueing $\operatorname{Spec} C$ to the chart at infinity: a point $z$ of $X$; the element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ obtained (`hϖz`) as the germ at $z$ of the global section that is the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase`; the hypothesis `hz` that $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of that stalk; a point $y'$ of `XFin`$=\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` sending $y'$ to $z$ (`hy'`); the same supersingularity condition for $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ (`hss'`); and `hy'y`, stating $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}=y$.
--
--   The Drinfeld-chart data consist of a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$ (adically complete for its maximal ideal), a ring homomorphism $\sigma_1\colon A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), power series $f_1,u_1,v_1\in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form $X_0X_1^{\,q}-X_0^{\,q}X_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e_1\colon \widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;S:=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v_1-f_1u_1\big),$$
--   where $\widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}$ is the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ for its maximal ideal. Write `toC` for the map from the stalk to its completion, `mkS` for the quotient map onto $S$, and `germY` for the composite $C\to\mathcal O_{X,z}$ through the germ at $z$ on the image open set of `ιFin`.
--
--   The hypothesis `hW₁` is a conjunction of seven clauses, summarised here. (i) For every $a\in A$, $e_1$ sends the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ of the section coming from $a$ to $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1 a))$. (ii) For every $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — i.e. $\tau$ realises the $\gamma^{-1}$-slash action on quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(N_0)$, after complexification along any embedding sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$ — the automorphism $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$. (iii) If moreover $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, then the induced automorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$. (iv) For $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving $C$ and acting trivially modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W_1$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W_1)$ such that $\theta$ conjugates the action of $\tau$ on $C$ through $e_1\circ\,$`toC`$\,\circ\,$`germY`, $\theta$ fixes all constants $C(w)$, $\theta(\mathrm{mk}_S X_j)\equiv\sum_i \mathrm{mk}_S(C(M_{ij})X_i)$ modulo $(\mathrm{mk}_SX_0,\mathrm{mk}_SX_1)^2$, $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$ and $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$, $c\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c\not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$. (v) A branch-distinctness clause: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting at least one of $\mathrm{mk}_SX_0,\mathrm{mk}_SX_1$, both containing $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$, and each containing an element $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along `toC` followed by $e_1$ are distinct ideals of the stalk. (vi) A branch-anchor clause: for every prime $P$ of $S$ omitting one of $\mathrm{mk}_SX_0,\mathrm{mk}_SX_1$, containing $\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$, and containing an element $1\cdot X_0+0\cdot X_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and for every $a\in C$: the image `toC (germY a)` lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e_1$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ (as an element of $L((T))$) lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ under $A\to L$. (vii) A Hasse-chart clause asserting that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and that there are $a_0\in A$ with the difference of that element and $a_0$ in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0\ge 1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b\in W_1$, at least one of them a unit, with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}$, the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{\,e_0-i}$ is a unit, and such that $e_1$ carries the germ of that difference to $\mathrm{mk}_S h$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion asserts the existence of an ideal $G$ of $C$ with the following five properties: $G$ is prime; for every $a\in C$, $a\in G$ if and only if for every $n\in\mathbb Z$ the $n$-th Laurent coefficient of $a$ equals the image under $A\to L$ of some element of $\mathfrak m_A$; the image of $\varpi$ under $A\to C$ lies in $G$; $G\le y$; and $G\neq y$.
--
--   The ideal characterised by the coefficient condition is the Gauss prime of the chart algebra cut out by requiring all $q$-expansion coefficients to be non-units, that is, the generic point of the Igusa component through the cusp; the statement says that, given a Drinfeld-chart presentation of the completed local ring at a supersingular point of the two-chart integral model, this ideal is prime and is contained strictly in the supersingular maximal ideal $y$. It is proved from the branch analysis [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.branchPrimes_of_sub_drinfeldForm_mem_pow`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.branchPrimes_of_sub_drinfeldForm_mem_pow) together with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.comap_eq_and_dense_and_flat_drinfeldChartWitness_chartAlgFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.comap_eq_and_dense_and_flat_drinfeldChartWitness_chartAlgFin), and feeds the Igusa-type and level-automorphism statements [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_isPrime_forall_igusaType_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_of_end_blowupChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_isPrime_forall_igusaType_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_of_end_blowupChart) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.forall_coeff_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_of_isLevelAutAt_gamma_of_drinfeldChartWitness`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.forall_coeff_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_of_isLevelAutAt_gamma_of_drinfeldChartWitness).
